From cb9c221f4a140b557b417e653260dcaa00453860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:24:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper: USB mount chain - dnsmasq survives a late volume, a
 reboot releases the volumes and their swap, a mount watchdog, the soft-lockup
 panic re-armed once the box has settled

Field (RT-BE86U, Entware + amtm on a USB SSD, 2026-10-02): the LAN had no DNS
or DHCP after a boot until the volume mounted, a volume whose first mount failed
never mounted, and USB that was fine after a flash came back dirty after a GUI
reboot. Stock's boot order and caps cause all three; none is a Reaper regression
(checked against the v3.2.9 e2fsprogs CVE change and the v3.2.3 boot polls).

Boot:
- start_dnsmasq(): reaper_dnsmasq_log_guard() drops a log-facility, conf-file or
  conf-dir whose path is not there yet - the storage drivers load AFTER
  start_services, so a postconf pointing at /opt killed dnsmasq "cannot open
  log" on every boot. Each drop is logged and recorded in
  REAPER_DNSMASQ_LOGDROP_FLAG; watchdog's dnsmasq_check() restarts dnsmasq once
  the dependency exists. Both sides judge with reaper_dnsmasq_dep_missing(), so
  a restart is never re-dropped.
- pre-mount: run_custom_script_bounded() (shared/scripts.c, reaper_wait_pgrp)
  stops the script AND its process group at the cap. Stock's alarm() killed the
  shell only and left an e2fsck holding the device O_EXCL, so the mount that
  followed failed EBUSY for good. The cap is 300 s: amtm's disk check waits
  ~60 s for NTP before a full e2fsck of a dirty SSD even starts.
- mount_r(): EBUSY is waited out (up to 120 s) instead of abandoned. The hotplug
  add is one-shot, so a mount that failed there was never retried.

Reboot:
- init's SIGTERM/SIGQUIT path runs `reaper_usb_release reboot` BEFORE
  stop_services(): services-stop to completion, the holder sweep, then swapoff
  of every swap under /tmp/mnt (usbrel_swaps_under). The swap file is the one
  holder no process sweep clears and it survives shutdn()'s kill -1, so a lazily
  detached volume with amtm's swap on it rebooted dirty. stop_services() skips
  its own background services-stop while REAPER_USBREL_FLAG says the release
  already ran. SIGHUP (restart services) keeps the volumes.
- Soft-lockup panic: this kernel has BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC=y, so a 20 s
  I/O stall (swap to a USB disk through the post-mount storm on a 1 GB box) is
  a reboot with no trace. init writes softlockup_panic=0 at boot, usb.c writes 0
  and stamps the uptime around every mount (reaper_usb_mount_stamp), and the
  watchdog re-arms 1 once the box is up >= 600 s and >= 300 s past the last
  stamp (reaper_slp_should_arm; REAPER_SLP_* in rc.h). A truly hung box is
  still reset by the hardware watchdog. panic_on_oops is unchanged.
- rc/reaper_usbmon.c, on the watchdog tick at a 30 s cadence: re-sends the
  block add event for an attached partition never mounted since boot (3 tries,
  30 s apart, within 30 min of boot or the last mount activity, usb lock free; a
  GUI eject is never touched); clears a release flag older than 10 min with no
  image waiting (an aborted flash) and gives the volumes back; once at 600 s, on
  a box that expects a volume (post-mount exists) and has no USB WAN,
  re-enumerates a storage device that produced no disk - RT-BE96U and RT-BE86U
  have no USB power control (pwr_usb_gpio 0xff), so a wedged UAS enclosure is
  never power-cycled. That path is logged UNTESTED.

Riding in the same files: watchdog.c publishes bondst only when it changes
(perf audit P35a - an nvram write every 10 s for an unchanging value); init.c
calls the closed slabdbg() only with nvram dbg=1 (stock dumped ~230 lines of
meminfo, free, slabinfo and bpm status into syslog on every boot).

Metal: RT-BE96U r2/r3/r4 - flash boot and GUI reboot clean, volume mounted
first try at ~95 s, "soft-lockup panic armed: up 624 s, no USB mount activity
for 530 s", every new path correctly idle. Field r2 (the reporter's box): four
retries, waited for the mount. The Entware box's GUI reboot on r4 (the swapoff
branch) is still owed.

Tests: build-scripts/tests/test_usb_boot_mount.py (56 checks),
test_usb_flash_release.py (16) and test_usb_late_mount.py (36) compile the
libc-only pieces on the host and run them; verify_markers lines for each path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
